    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42398" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltātus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		salto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a</i> (religious) <i>dance</i> (not ante-Aug.,
			and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Numa Salios) per urbem ire canentes carmina
					cum tripudiis sollennique saltatu jussit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
					20</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Sen. Troad. 786</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 21 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltatibus apta juventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 14, 637</span></i>
			.</div>
